    "summary": "Iconic HCS > China > Rider trio with tight jams and stellar playing",
    "blurb": "The concert shines with the blistering Here Comes Sunshine → China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider sequence and strong renditions of Box of Rain, Bird Song and Playing In The Band. Jerry’s soaring solos and Phil’s thunderous bass drive the marathon set while Keith adds tasteful piano touches. Overall it’s a high‑energy early‑’73 highlight.",
    "review": "On February 17, 1973 at St. Paul Auditorium the Dead delivered one of their classic early‑'70s marathons. The first set rolled through a tight mix of new material and staples—The Promised Land, Looks Like Rain, Box of Rain and a soulful Playing In The Band that built momentum for an explosive second half. The centerpiece is the legendary Here Comes Sunshine → China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider sandwich, where Jerry’s metallic Strat tone and white‑hot runs cut through the mix while Phil Lesh’s fire‑hot bass propels the jam forward. Keith Godchaux’s rag‑time piano adds melodic sparkle on songs like Looks Like Rain, and the dual drummers lay down a solid, driving groove that keeps the energy high through Truckin’, Row Jimmy and the encore. The Ashley‑field soundboard capture (gd1973-02-17.sbd.ashley-field.32875.sbeok.flac16) presents crystal‑clear instrument separation despite a few tape glitches, making this performance an essential listen for any Deadhead.",
